---
import DocsLayout from '../../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Stereo Workflow — MHA Manager"
  description="Process stereo HMC footage end to end: the calibration -> identity -> performance chain, depth generation, the solve, and export."
  currentSlug="stereo-workflow"
>

  <div class="doc-header">
    <span class="type-badge type-stereo">Stereo</span>
    <h1 class="doc-title">Stereo Workflow</h1>
    <p class="doc-lead">
      Stereo (HMC) is the highest-fidelity job type — the depth-constrained solve resolves facial
      geometry that monocular footage cannot. In exchange each take needs two parent assets for its
      actor first: a <strong>camera calibration</strong> and a prepared
      <strong>MetaHuman Identity</strong>. The queue produces both and chains them for you.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="type-section">
    <h2 class="sub-heading">Pipeline stages</h2>
    <div class="fork">
      <div class="fork-branches">
        <div class="fork-branch">
          <span class="branch-tag">Requires</span>
          <div class="pipeline">
            <div class="pipeline-stage node-calib"><span class="stage-name">Camera Calibration Create</span><span class="stage-note">CalibrateStereo</span></div>
            <div class="pipeline-arrow">-&gt;</div>
            <div class="pipeline-stage node-identity"><span class="stage-name">Identity Create</span><span class="stage-note">MHID_&lt;Actor&gt;</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="lane-drop"><span class="drop-arrow">&#8595;</span></div>
        <div class="fork-branch">
          <span class="branch-tag">Then solves</span>
          <div class="pipeline">
            <div class="pipeline-stage"><span class="stage-name">Validate Input</span></div>
            <div class="pipeline-arrow">-&gt;</div>
            <div class="pipeline-stage highlight"><span class="stage-name">Generate Depth</span><span class="stage-note">Stereo only</span></div>
            <div class="pipeline-arrow">-&gt;</div>
            <div class="pipeline-stage highlight"><span class="stage-name">Clean Depth</span><span class="stage-note">Optional</span></div>
            <div class="pipeline-arrow">-&gt;</div>
            <div class="pipeline-stage"><span class="stage-name">Process Performance</span></div>
            <div class="pipeline-arrow">-&gt;</div>
            <div class="pipeline-stage"><span class="stage-name">Export + Save</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="callout callout-note">
      <strong>Depth generation is serial.</strong> Even when Max Concurrent Jobs is above 1, depth
      generation for all stereo jobs completes before any job enters the concurrent processing pool.
      Depth is skipped when the take already has a linked depth sequence.
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="type-section">
    <h2 class="sub-heading">Required assets</h2>
    <div class="asset-table">
      <div class="asset-row header"><span>Asset</span><span>Type</span><span>Notes</span></div>
      <div class="asset-row">
        <span><strong>Capture Data</strong></span>
        <span><code>UFootageCaptureData</code></span>
        <span>Must reference both camera image sequences</span>
      </div>
      <div class="asset-row">
        <span><strong>Identity</strong></span>
        <span><code>UMetaHumanIdentity</code></span>
        <span>Auto-discovered under the actor folder; built by an Identity Create job</span>
      </div>
      <div class="asset-row">
        <span><strong>Camera Calibration</strong></span>
        <span><code>UCameraCalibration</code></span>
        <span>Required for depth generation; auto-discovered, or built by a Calibration job</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="type-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">The parent chain</h2>
    <p class="type-desc">
      Stereo is a family of three job types in a strict dependency order. The first two exist only to
      produce the assets the third consumes:
    </p>
    <div class="tier-table">
      <div class="tier-row header">
        <span>Tier</span><span>Job</span><span>Produces</span><span>Blocks until ready</span>
      </div>
      <div class="tier-row">
        <span>1</span>
        <span><strong>CalibrateStereo</strong></span>
        <span>A <code>CameraCalibration</code> from a checkerboard take, linked to the take and discoverable by the actor's other takes.</span>
        <span>-</span>
      </div>
      <div class="tier-row">
        <span>2</span>
        <span><strong>Identity Create</strong></span>
        <span>A rigged, prepared <code>MetaHumanIdentity</code> (<code>MHID_&lt;Actor&gt;</code>), built from an identity take using the calibration.</span>
        <span>Needs the calibration (for depth). Runs in an interactive editor (cloud AutoRig login).</span>
      </div>
      <div class="tier-row">
        <span>3</span>
        <span><strong>Stereo performance</strong></span>
        <span>A <code>Performance</code> asset + face <code>AnimSequence</code> — a depth-constrained solve.</span>
        <span>Needs <strong>both</strong> the calibration and the prepared identity for its actor.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="callout callout-note">
      <strong>The iron rule:</strong> a stereo take never processes without both parent assets for its
      actor. Depth is generated from the calibration before the solve, so a bad calibration would
      poison every take built on it — which is why the calibration quality gates sit upstream. Mono
      and Audio jobs depend on neither and never wait.
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="type-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Queue in any order</h2>
    <p class="type-desc">
      Execution ignores row order: the batch runs <strong>CalibrateStereo first, Identity Create
      second, everything else third</strong>, so prerequisites exist by the time a take preflights.
      The queue is strictly serial (Epic's single-performance lock), and takes classify by name —
      <code>grid</code> / <code>calib</code> tokens become CalibrateStereo, <code>identity</code> /
      <code>dna</code> become Identity Create. Drop a whole actor folder in at once and let the tiers
      sort themselves out.
    </p>
    <div class="callout callout-tip">
      <strong>Worked example.</strong> Queue everything under <code>Imports/Aaron/</code> in any order
      and press Start:
      <ol class="inline-list">
        <li><code>Aaron_Calib_Grid</code> runs first (CalibrateStereo) -&gt; a Camera Calibration next to the take.</li>
        <li><code>Aaron_Identity_DNA</code> runs second (Identity Create): depth with that calibration -&gt; neutral track -&gt; conform -&gt; AutoRig -&gt; <code>MHID_Aaron</code>.</li>
        <li><code>Aaron_Take01..N</code> run last (Stereo): preflight links the calibration and <code>MHID_Aaron</code>, and each take produces a Performance + AnimSequence.</li>
        <li>Takes queued before their prerequisites simply wait as a blocked status and resume automatically once the parent completes.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="type-section">
    <h2 class="sub-heading">Stereo-specific options</h2>
    <div class="option-list">
      <div class="option-row">
        <span class="option-name">Solve Type</span>
        <span class="option-desc">Selects the internal stereo solver variant. Leave at default unless directed by Epic support.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="option-row">
        <span class="option-name">Head Movement Reference Frame</span>
        <span class="option-desc">Frame used as the identity reference for head-movement correction. Set to a neutral, stable, forward-facing frame.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="option-row">
        <span class="option-name">Face Coverage / Width Thresholds</span>
        <span class="option-desc">Minimum proportion of the face visible in depth, and minimum face width in depth pixels, for a frame to be used. Raise to filter partial-face or too-distant frames.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="option-row">
        <span class="option-name">Baseline / Scale Tolerance</span>
        <span class="option-desc">Acceptable deviation between the calibrated stereo geometry and the live footage. Increase if the rig was adjusted between calibration and capture.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="callout callout-tip">
      See <a href="/marketplace/mha-manager/docs/job-options#stereo">Per-Job Options</a> for the full
      stereo parameter reference.
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="type-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Depth Clean-Up Pass</h2>
    <p class="type-desc">
      An optional <strong>Clean Depth</strong> stage between depth generation and the solve. It is not
      a blur or global denoise — it distinguishes background from subject by flood-filling inward from
      the image border, then patches only genuine interior gaps (dropouts inside the face/body
      silhouette) with a distance-weighted average of surrounding valid depth. Background and
      out-of-range pixels are left alone rather than smeared.
    </p>
    <div class="option-list">
      <div class="option-row">
        <span class="option-name">Non-destructive</span>
        <span class="option-desc">Writes a new copy of the depth sequence - package suffix <code>_Clean</code>, sibling <code>_clean</code> directory on disk - so the original capture data is never modified.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="option-row">
        <span class="option-name">Asynchronous</span>
        <span class="option-desc">EXR I/O and pixel work run on the thread pool, not the game thread — the editor stays responsive and the pass is cancellable mid-run.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="option-row">
        <span class="option-name">Idempotent</span>
        <span class="option-desc">Re-running a job that already has a cleaned sequence re-cleans from the newest source rather than stacking passes.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="type-section" id="calibration-identity">
    <h2 class="section-title">Calibration &amp; Identity jobs</h2>
    <h3 class="sub-heading">Stereo Calibration</h3>
    <p class="type-desc">
      Right-click a checkerboard take and choose <strong>Generate Stereo Calibration (Checkerboard
      Take)</strong>, or let name tokens (<code>grid</code>/<code>calib</code>) classify it. It drives
      Epic's MetaHuman Calibration Processing plugin (UE 5.7+) and produces a
      <code>CC_&lt;TakeName&gt;</code> asset linked to the Capture Data, plus an optional OpenCV
      <code>calib.json</code> on disk. The board is measured in <strong>squares</strong>, not inner
      corners (Epic's shipped board is 11 x 16 at 0.75 cm), and Auto-Detect probes candidate sizes
      before the full scan. Frame selection, sharpness, board override, and the quality gates live
      under <a href="/marketplace/mha-manager/docs/global-settings">Global Settings -&gt; Stereo Calibration</a>.
    </p>
    <h3 class="sub-heading">Identity Create</h3>
    <p class="type-desc">
      Right-click a stereo identity take and choose <strong>Create MetaHuman Identity (Stereo)</strong>,
      or let <code>identity</code>/<code>dna</code> tokens classify it. It generates depth, tracks the
      neutral frame, conforms the template mesh, runs Epic's cloud AutoRig, and prepares the identity
      for performance (<code>MHID_&lt;Actor&gt;</code>). A finished identity is reused across the
      actor's takes — delete the asset to force a rebuild.
    </p>
    <div class="callout callout-note">
      Identity Create needs an interactive editor session for the cloud AutoRig login, so it is
      <strong>not available in headless / CI runs</strong>. Build identities in the editor first, then
      batch the performance solves.
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="type-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Discovery and blocked states</h2>
    <p class="type-desc">
      Discovery is scoped to the actor's folders, which is why keeping a shoot's takes under one actor
      folder matters:
    </p>
    <ul class="bullet-list">
      <li><strong>Calibration lookup:</strong> already linked on the Capture Data -&gt; capture parent folder -&gt; take folder -&gt; sibling take folders -&gt; one level higher, never past <code>/Game</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Identity lookup:</strong> capture parent folder -&gt; actor folder, preferring <code>MHID_&lt;Actor&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Rejected calibrations</strong> (set aside for poor quality) are invisible to every lookup until you accept or re-solve them.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="tier-table" style="margin-top: 16px;">
      <div class="blk-row header"><span>Status</span><span>Meaning &amp; how it clears</span></div>
      <div class="blk-row">
        <span><strong>MissingCalibration</strong></span>
        <span>No calibration found for the actor yet. Requeues automatically the moment one appears (a Calibration job finishes, or you link the asset).</span>
      </div>
      <div class="blk-row">
        <span><strong>MissingIdentity</strong></span>
        <span>No prepared identity found for the actor yet. Requeues automatically once one exists.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="blk-row">
        <span><strong>PoorCalibrationQuality</strong></span>
        <span>A calibration solved but exceeded a quality gate and was set aside. Waits for an explicit decision — <strong>Accept Anyway</strong>, or a better re-solve. See <a href="/marketplace/mha-manager/docs/global-settings">Calibration settings</a>.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .doc-header { margin-bottom: 40px; }

  .type-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 3px 10px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .type-stereo { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 12%, transparent); color: var(--accent); border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 30%, transparent); }

  .doc-title {
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.4rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .doc-lead {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    max-width: 620px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .doc-lead strong, .type-desc strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 500; }
  .doc-lead code, .type-desc code, .callout code, .asset-row code, .tier-row code, .blk-row code, .bullet-list code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .type-section {
    margin-bottom: 48px;
    padding-bottom: 48px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .type-section:last-of-type { border-bottom: none; }

  .type-desc {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.75;
    max-width: 640px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .sub-heading {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.07em;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin: 24px 0 10px;
  }
  .sub-heading:first-child { margin-top: 0; }

  .section-title {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .asset-table, .tier-table {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }

  .asset-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 1.3fr 1.4fr;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 10px 16px;
    font-size: 0.825rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .tier-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 0.4fr 1fr 2.2fr 2fr;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 12px 16px;
    font-size: 0.825rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    align-items: start;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .blk-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 3fr;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 11px 16px;
    font-size: 0.825rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    align-items: start;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .asset-row:last-child, .tier-row:last-child, .blk-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }

  .asset-row.header, .tier-row.header, .blk-row.header {
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .asset-row strong, .tier-row strong, .blk-row strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 500; }

  .pipeline {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    margin: 4px 0 12px;
  }

  .pipeline-stage {
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 7px 14px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
  }
  .pipeline-stage.highlight {
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, transparent);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 6%, transparent);
  }
  .stage-name { font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); }
  .stage-note { font-size: 0.7rem; color: var(--accent); }
  .pipeline-arrow { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); }

  .fork {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 14px;
    margin: 4px 0 12px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .fork-source { flex-shrink: 0; }

  .fork-branches {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
    border-left: 2px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 40%, transparent);
    padding-left: 16px;
  }

  .fork-branch {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .branch-tag {
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    min-width: 74px;
  }

  .lane-drop {
    padding-left: 84px;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .drop-arrow {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 1.3rem;
  }

  .pipeline-stage.node-calib {
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, #f0a500 45%, transparent);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, #f0a500 9%, transparent);
  }
  .pipeline-stage.node-calib .stage-name,
  .pipeline-stage.node-calib .stage-note { color: #f0a500; }

  .pipeline-stage.node-identity {
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, #4ade80 45%, transparent);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, #4ade80 9%, transparent);
  }
  .pipeline-stage.node-identity .stage-name,
  .pipeline-stage.node-identity .stage-note { color: #4ade80; }

  .option-list {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .option-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 2fr;
    gap: 20px;
    padding: 12px 16px;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .option-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .option-name { font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); font-size: 0.825rem; }
  .option-desc { color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.5; }

  .bullet-list {
    padding-left: 20px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .bullet-list li { font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.6; padding-left: 4px; }
  .bullet-list li strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 500; }

  .inline-list {
    margin: 10px 0 0;
    padding-left: 20px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
  }
  .inline-list li { line-height: 1.55; }

  .callout {
    padding: 14px 18px;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 16px 0 0;
    border-left: 3px solid;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .callout-tip  { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 8%, transparent); border-color: var(--accent); }
  .callout-note { background: color-mix(in srgb, #f0a500 8%, transparent); border-color: #f0a500; }
  .callout strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }
  .callout code { color: var(--accent); }

  a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .asset-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
    .asset-row span:last-child, .asset-row.header span:last-child { display: none; }
    .tier-row { grid-template-columns: 0.4fr 1fr; gap: 4px 12px; }
    .tier-row span:nth-child(3), .tier-row span:nth-child(4) { grid-column: 2; }
    .tier-row.header span:nth-child(3), .tier-row.header span:nth-child(4) { display: none; }
    .blk-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 4px; }
    .option-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 4px; }
  }
</style>
